{
  "id": "al3",
  "title": "Octal",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "al3-l1",
      "title": "Groups of Three",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Long rows of 0s and 1s are hard to read. So Altair programmers grouped the bits in threes, from the right: 01 111 110.",
        "Three bits make one octal digit, from 0 (000) to 7 (111). 01 111 110 becomes 1 7 6: octal 176. A byte goes from octal 000 to 377.",
        "The Altair's front panel even marked the switches in groups of three."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "00 111 110   ; MVI A",
          "10 101 010   ; octal 252",
          "11 010 011   ; OUT",
          "11 111 111   ; port 377: the lights",
          "01 110 110   ; HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ●○●○●○●○ = 170"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al3-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is 101 as an octal digit?",
          "options": [
            "5",
            "3",
            "101",
            "6"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "4 + 1 = 5."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is 11 111 111 in octal?",
          "options": [
            "377",
            "777",
            "255",
            "11111111"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "3, 7, 7."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l1-e3",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to octal 052.",
          "answer": 42,
          "explanation": "0 = 00, 5 = 101, 2 = 010: 00 101 010."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l1-e4",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "01 000 111 in octal is ___",
          "code": [
            "01 000 111 = ___"
          ],
          "options": [
            "107",
            "147",
            "71",
            "017"
          ],
          "answer": "107",
          "explanation": "1, 0, 7."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l1-e5",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to octal 300.",
          "answer": 192,
          "explanation": "3 = 11, then 000 000: the two top switches up."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why did programmers like octal?",
          "options": [
            "One digit is exactly three switches",
            "It's shorter than decimal",
            "The 8080 can't count in decimal",
            "It's from the Romans"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Reading 076 is easier than 00111110."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "al3-l2",
      "title": "Why the 8080 Loves Octal",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Look at MVI in octal: MVI A is 076, MVI B is 006, MVI C is 016. The middle digit is the register! The 8080 numbers its registers 0 to 7: B 0, C 1, D 2, E 3, H 4, L 5, M 6 (memory) and A 7.",
        "So MVI r is always 0 r 6 in octal: 00 rrr 110 in binary. HLT is 166, OUT 323, ADI 306, SUI 326.",
        "Once you know the pattern, you can work out instructions in your head. That's why 8080 programmers thought in octal."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "00 000 110   ; 006: MVI B",
          "00 001 001   ; 9",
          "00 111 110   ; 076: MVI A",
          "00 000 001   ; 1",
          "11 010 011   ; 323: OUT",
          "11 111 111   ; 377: the lights",
          "01 110 110   ; 166: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○○○○● = 1"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al3-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Which register is number 7?",
          "options": [
            "A",
            "B",
            "M",
            "L"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A, the accumulator, is 7."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "MVI A is 076. What is MVI B?",
          "options": [
            "006",
            "076",
            "106",
            "060"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "B is register 0: 0 0 6."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l2-e3",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to MVI C (0 1 6).",
          "answer": 14,
          "explanation": "00 001 110: C is register 1."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l2-e4",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "The octal code for HLT is ___",
          "code": [
            "HLT = ___"
          ],
          "options": [
            "166",
            "076",
            "323",
            "377"
          ],
          "answer": "166",
          "explanation": "01 110 110."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does the middle octal digit of MVI tell you?",
          "options": [
            "Which register gets the value",
            "The value itself",
            "The port",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "MVI r = 0 r 6."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l2-e6",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to MVI E.",
          "answer": 30,
          "explanation": "E is register 3: 0 3 6 = 00 011 110."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "al3-l3",
      "title": "Writing in Octal",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "In this app, a byte can be written as 3 octal digits instead of 8 bits: 076 means the same as 00 111 110.",
        "Programs from the 70s were printed like that: long lists of three-digit octal numbers that people toggled in by hand.",
        "Careful: octal digits only go up to 7. 080 isn't octal, and a byte never goes above 377."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; MVI A",
          "052   ; octal 52 = 42",
          "323   ; OUT",
          "377   ; the lights",
          "166   ; HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○●○●○●○ = 42"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al3-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is 076 in binary?",
          "options": [
            "00 111 110",
            "01 110 110",
            "00 000 076",
            "11 111 110"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "0, 7 (111), 6 (110)."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l3-e2",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the octal program in order.",
          "lines": [
            "076   ; MVI A",
            "007   ; 7",
            "323   ; OUT",
            "377   ; the lights",
            "166   ; HLT"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "076   ; MVI A",
            "007   ; 7",
            "323   ; OUT",
            "377   ; the lights",
            "166   ; HLT"
          ],
          "explanation": "MVI A and its value, OUT and its port, HLT."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l3-e3",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program doesn't load. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "076   ; MVI A",
            "089   ; the value",
            "323   ; OUT",
            "377   ; the lights",
            "166   ; HLT"
          ],
          "answer": 1,
          "explanation": "8 and 9 aren't octal digits."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l3-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What do the lights show for 076, 077, 323, 377, 166?",
          "options": [
            "○○●●●●●● = 63",
            "○○○○○●●● = 7",
            "●●●●●●●● = 255",
            "nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "077 octal = 63 = 00 111 111."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l3-e5",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "The value byte is 125 in octal. Set the switches to it.",
          "answer": 85,
          "explanation": "1 = 01, 2 = 010, 5 = 101: 01 010 101."
        },
        {
          "id": "al3-l3-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Which is the biggest byte in octal?",
          "options": [
            "377",
            "777",
            "255",
            "999"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "11 111 111 = 3 7 7."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
